                <pb facs="0632" n="542" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg542"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2730</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-09-21T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 21,
                                1918, 4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>267. Referring to the action of General
                        Poole and resultant friction with Russians, I understand
                        Lindley has been advised of this
                    Government’s views and of action by British Government both as to the future
                    course of General Poole and to correct
                    the unfortunate impression made at Archangel.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
